# TikTok LIVE API SDK for Python

[![PyPI version](https://img.shields.io/pypi/v/{{ project_name }}?color=0274b5)](https://pypi.org/project/{{ project_name }}/)
[![PyPI downloads](https://img.shields.io/pypi/dm/{{ project_name }})](https://pypi.org/project/{{ project_name }}/)
[![Python versions](https://img.shields.io/pypi/pyversions/{{ project_name }})](https://pypi.org/project/{{ project_name }}/)
[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-green)](https://github.com/EulerStream/TikTok-Live-Api/blob/master/LICENSE)
[![Discord](https://img.shields.io/badge/Discord-join-5865F2)](https://www.eulerstream.com/discord)

`{{ project_name }}` is the official Python client for the [EulerStream TikTok LIVE API](https://www.eulerstream.com). Connect to any TikTok LIVE stream by `@username` and receive real-time **chat messages, gifts, likes, follows, shares, viewer counts, room stats and PK battles** over a managed WebSocket, plus fully typed sync and async clients for webcast signing, LIVE rooms, gifts, rankings, LIVE alerts, moderation, captchas and analytics.

EulerStream is the managed TikTok LIVE backend behind [TikTokLive](https://github.com/isaackogan/TikTokLive), the most popular Python library for TikTok LIVE. The connection layer is hosted and maintained for you, so your integration keeps working when TikTok changes its webcast protocol.

> Unofficial: this project is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to TikTok or ByteDance.

## Installation

```bash
pip install {{ project_name }}
```

Requires Python 3.10+. Built on [httpx](https://www.python-httpx.org/) and [attrs](https://www.attrs.org/); every endpoint has `sync`, `sync_detailed`, `asyncio` and `asyncio_detailed` variants and ships with full type hints (`py.typed`).

## Quick start

1. [Create a free EulerStream account](https://www.eulerstream.com/register) (no credit card required)
2. Copy your API key from the dashboard
3. Make your first calls:

```python
from {{ package_name }} import AuthenticatedClient
from {{ package_name }}.api.tik_tok_users import retrieve_tik_tok_user_basic
from {{ package_name }}.api.tik_tok_live_gifts import list_webcast_gifts
from {{ package_name }}.api.tik_tok_live_rooms import fetch_webcast_url

client = AuthenticatedClient(base_url="https://api.eulerstream.com", token="YOUR_API_KEY")

with client as c:
    # Look up any TikTok user by @username
    user = retrieve_tik_tok_user_basic.sync(unique_id="tv_asahi_news", client=c)
    print(user.user.nickname)

    # Browse the TikTok LIVE gift catalog (names, diamond values, images)
    catalog = list_webcast_gifts.sync(client=c)
    for gift in catalog.gifts:
        print(f"{gift.gift_name} = {gift.diamond_count} diamonds")

    # Fetch the TikTok LIVE WebSocket URL + first payload for a LIVE room (protobuf)
    webcast = fetch_webcast_url.sync_detailed(room_id="7318296342189919018", client=c)
    print(webcast.status_code)
```

The same calls with asyncio:

```python
import asyncio
from {{ package_name }} import AuthenticatedClient
from {{ package_name }}.api.tik_tok_users import retrieve_tik_tok_user_basic

async def main():
    async with AuthenticatedClient(base_url="https://api.eulerstream.com", token="YOUR_API_KEY") as c:
        user = await retrieve_tik_tok_user_basic.asyncio(unique_id="tv_asahi_news", client=c)
        print(user.user.nickname)

asyncio.run(main())
```

Business plans can resolve a LIVE room straight from the creator's `@username` with `{{ package_name }}.api.tik_tok_live_anchors.fetch_webcast_url_by_unique_id`. `AuthenticatedClient` sends your key in the `X-Api-Key` header; use `{{ package_name }}.Client` for the handful of routes that allow anonymous access.

## What you can build

- **Live stream overlays** for OBS and browser sources showing TikTok LIVE chat, gifts and top gifters
- **Gift and follow alerts** that trigger sounds, animations or webhooks in real time
- **TikTok LIVE games** controlled by chat commands or gifts
- **Chatbots and moderation tools** that respond to and moderate TikTok LIVE chat
- **Analytics dashboards** tracking diamonds, viewer retention and top supporters
- **LIVE monitoring**: bulk "is this creator live?" checks and LIVE start/end alerts for thousands of accounts

## API coverage

Every path/method in the [EulerStream OpenAPI spec](https://www.eulerstream.com/docs/openapi) becomes a module under `{{ package_name }}.api.<group>`, so the SDK always matches the live API.

| Module | TikTok LIVE API group |
|---|---|
| `api.tik_tok_live` | Core TikTok LIVE: bulk live checks, webcast feed, hashtag lists, rankings |
| `api.tik_tok_live_anchors` | Creators: webcast URL by `@username`, room info / ID / cover, gift gallery, earnings, moderators, LIVE analytics |
| `api.tik_tok_live_rooms` | LIVE rooms: webcast URL by room ID, room info, room gifts, send chat |
| `api.tik_tok_live_events` | TikTok LIVE event history for a creator |
| `api.tik_tok_live_gifts` | TikTok LIVE gift catalog: list, search and look up gifts |
| `api.tik_tok_live_rankings` | Creator leaderboards, rankings and ranking history |
| `api.tik_tok_live_agencies` | TikTok LIVE agency catalog |
| `api.tik_tok_live_alerts` / `api.tik_tok_live_alert_targets` | TikTok LIVE start/end alerts and webhook targets |
| `api.tik_tok_live_moderation` | Kicks, bans, mutes, sensitive words and comment toggles |
| `api.tik_tok_signing` | TikTok request signing and payload decryption |
| `api.tik_tok_captchas` | TikTok captcha solving |
| `api.tik_tok_general` | TikTok OAuth: token exchange, introspection, revocation, user info |
| `api.tik_tok_users` / `api.tik_tok_videos` | TikTok user profiles and videos |
| `api.tik_tok_web_socket_api` | Your cloud WebSocket connections and their state |
| `api.accounts` / `api.authentication` / `api.analytics` | Your EulerStream account, API keys, JWTs and usage analytics |

Per-endpoint Python examples for every operation are in the [EulerStream API docs](https://www.eulerstream.com/docs/intro).

## Advanced usage

Customize the underlying `httpx.Client` / `httpx.AsyncClient` (timeouts, proxies, event hooks) through `httpx_args`, or replace it entirely:

```python
import httpx
from {{ package_name }} import AuthenticatedClient

client = AuthenticatedClient(
    base_url="https://api.eulerstream.com",
    token="YOUR_API_KEY",
    timeout=httpx.Timeout(30),
    httpx_args={"proxy": "http://localhost:8030"},
)
```

See the docstrings on `Client` and `AuthenticatedClient` for every option, including `verify_ssl`, `raise_on_unexpected_status` and `follow_redirects`.

## Other languages

The TikTok LIVE API SDK is also available for [Node.js / TypeScript](https://www.npmjs.com/package/tiktok-live-api-sdk), [C# / .NET](https://www.nuget.org/packages/EulerApiSdk), [Java](https://central.sonatype.com/artifact/com.eulerstream/euler-api-sdk) and [Go](https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/EulerStream/TikTok-Live-Api/sdk/go), and anything else can use the language-agnostic WebSocket directly.

